      "text": {
        "id": 44,
        "title": "Dapper Liam and Noel, experimental Björk, and Bowie ‘cuddling himself’: Rankin reveals his never-before-seen shots of the stars",
        "source": "The Guardian - Culture",
        "source_id": "guardian_culture",
        "category": "culture",
        "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2026/nov/23/rankin-photographer-interview-contact-david-bowie-oasis",
        "published_at": "2026-11-23T08:00:50",
        "level": "A2",
        "slot_level": "A2",
        "source_level": "B1",
        "word_count": 954,
        "duration_sec": null,
        "body_text": "“I hate AI,” says Rankin. “A lot of people think I’m an evangelical twat about it, and I’m not. I think it’s disgusting. I think the people who run it are disgusting. They’ve made a massive gamble with humanity and society and culture.” His contempt may surprise anyone who’s familiar with Rankin’s substantial AI output.",
        "audio_url": null,
        "description": null,
        "license": "proprietary",
        "attribution": null,
        "truncated": true,
        "guid_hash": "4317d15d5e21d407dd0451da551a23b31471a352",
        "summary": "After some satirical experiments with the ‘disgusting’ AI, the photographer has returned to his first love with a book of contact sheets from his celebrity shoots. ‘I wish we could go back and stop everything changing,’ he says “I hate AI,” says Rankin. “A lot of people think I’m an evangelical twat about it, and I’m not. I think it’s disgusting. I think the people who run it are disgusting. They’ve made a massive gamble with humanity and society and culture.” His contempt may surprise anyone who’s familiar with Rankin’s substantial AI output. Ever since the artist Damien Hirst introduced him to the possibilities of generative AI in 2021, the British photographer has been going further down the rabbit hole. “I’m not somebody who likes to be critical about something without actually knowing about it,” he explains. “I’ve gone deep into trying to work it out.”",
